From: BlenderDesign Certification <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:18:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Retain certified Blender operation policy

Keep the reviewed live-versus-background routing guidance and visible staged-modeling progress contract that are present in the currently certified distribution.
---
 mcp/blmcp/data/prompts.yml | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mcp/blmcp/data/prompts.yml b/mcp/blmcp/data/prompts.yml
index 78dc537..4c87ca3 100644
--- a/mcp/blmcp/data/prompts.yml
+++ b/mcp/blmcp/data/prompts.yml
@@ -21,11 +21,34 @@ initial_instructions: |
 
   # Executing Code
 
+  ## Background and Live Routing
+
+  Use the `_for_cli` summary tools by default when the caller supplies a saved
+  `.blend` path and on-disk state is sufficient. Use `execute_blender_code_for_cli` for disposable batch work that must not modify the current open scene. Background
+  Blender has startup overhead and no window, area, or other interactive UI context.
+
+  Use live tools when unsaved state or UI context is required. Only use `execute_blender_code` to modify the current open scene. A `_for_cli` summary reads
+  the file on disk; its live counterpart reads the connected Blender instance.
+
   The `execute_blender_code` tool runs Python code via `bpy` in the connected Blender instance.
 
   The `execute_blender_code` tool is a last resort, if there are other tools that provide
   the functionality you need, use those instead.
 
+  # Visible Modeling Progress
+
+  For user-facing modeling or scene-building requests, create each distinct model part in
+  its own visible stage by default. Use a separate MCP tool call for each part, then let
+  Blender redraw and inspect the visible result before creating the next part.
+
+  After each stage, show the user the visible result (normally a viewport screenshot) and
+  a concise progress update, then continue automatically without waiting for user confirmation.
+  Only pause between stages when the user explicitly asks to review or approve each stage.
+
+  Do not create multiple model parts in one `execute_blender_code` call unless the user
+  explicitly asks for a one-shot or batch operation. Apply materials, assemble parts, and
+  perform the final visual audit in separate visible stages after the geometry parts.
+
   Prefer operators (`bpy.ops`) for standard actions (adding primitives, applying modifiers,
   setting origins) - they handle defaults and context. Use the data API (`bpy.data`) for
   precise control or to avoid side effects.
